    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0071" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Prime Minister
                        Churchill</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d26-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-08-19">August 19, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret to the Prime Minister from Harry L. Hopkins.</p>
                <p>The President wishes to discuss military requirements for Phase II with you at
                    your next meeting. This means that this matter is in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >status quo</hi> here for the present.</p>
                <p>I am looking forward to seeing you and hope you are well.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d26-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d26-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission not indicated. This message was sent in reply to
                    Churchill’s telegram of August 10, 1944, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg16">p. 16</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
